WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.240
I’m often asked
what my opinion

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.720
about a diet
or disease is.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:15.040
Who cares what my or
anyone else’s opinion is.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.640
All we should care about
is what the science says.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.280
What does the best available
balance of evidence

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.200
Published in the peer-
reviewed medical literature

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.560
have to say right now?

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.000
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.480
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:34.560
Today, we examine the best
way to have the most regular

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.440
and otherwise agreeable
bowel movements.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.560
And we’re going to start with
the best pooping position.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.400
While squatting continues
to be the traditional position

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.600
in populations of Asia and Africa,
Westerners have become

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.800
accustomed to sitting on toilet
seats. And when we do that,

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.600
when we sit upright,
our poop is forced to make

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.840
a nearly 90-degree turn,
the so-called recto-anal angle.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.920
Now, that's a good
thing in terms of

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.480
keeping us from pooping our
pants every time we sit down.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.560
But when it comes to doing our
business, the sitting toilet posture

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.120
defeats the purpose of our
body's brilliant design—

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.840
like trying to drive a car without
releasing the parking brake.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.800
Yet many physicians
are hesitant to discuss

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:19.280
such an unmentionable bodily
function or may just be ignorant.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.440
Doctors don't know squat.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.640
Of course, this is coming from
someone who owns a company

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.760
selling people squatting
platforms for their toilets.

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:31.120
In a previous video, I talked about
those little footstools you can use

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:33.840
to raise your knees when you
assume the pooping position,

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.560
but they were not found to
make a difference in terms

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.960
of self-described
difficulty in defecating

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.760
or the average time spent
emptying one's bowels.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.800
But those stools give only
a measly 4-inch boost.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.160
The so-called Squatty Potty
is twice that height,

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:50.720
and while you have to
admire their graphics,

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:56.480
from booty blockage to fecal fiesta,
complete with little rainbow poops,

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:01.760
it had never been put
to the test until now.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.680
The Implementation of
a Defecation Posture

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.000
Modification Device, i.e.,
Squatty Potty, and it worked!

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.640
Increased feelings of bowel
emptiness, reduced straining,

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.360
and about a minute off of
their on-the-pot reading time.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.640
The only downside
is the discomfort.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.560
Even just a 6-inch riser was found
to cause such extreme discomfort

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.160
in research subjects
in a previous trial,

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.400
they'd abandoned even
trying to study it.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.720
How else could we get that
same change in angle you get

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.320
from raising your feet?
How about just tipping forward?

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.920
Look familiar? It's like that famous
sculpture by Rodin, The Thinker.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.880
And indeed, Cleveland Clinic
researchers set out to study

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:44.080
"The Thinker" position for
defecation, and were able to show

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:47.760
an opening of the ano-rectal
angle, as measured using

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.200
cinedefecography—your
S.A.T. word for the day,

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.000
meaning basically
x-ray poop movie—

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.440
opening to more than 130
degrees, better than what

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.040
you can get just raising your feet,
which is only around 90 degrees.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:05.120
So "The Thinker" position may be a
more efficient method for defecation.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.880
and may help with constipation,

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.920
but it has not yet been
formally put to the test.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.080
As an aside, you can imagine
how the worst position might be

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.080
flat on your back using a bedpan,
because the spike in blood pressure

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:20.880
in your heart and brain when
you bear down, straining at stool,

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:24.320
is associated with sudden death
from heart attack and stroke.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:27.520
In fact, it's been found to be the
most common activity of daily living

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:30.400
being performed at the
time of death in Japan.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:34.720
And those who can't get out of bed
would seem to be especially at risk.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:38.640
That's why, if at all possible,
it can help to sit people up in bed

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.800
to cause less strain on the system.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:45.280
It's important to take a step back,
though, in this sitting vs. squatting

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:48.480
debate as this commentary
did nearly 50 years ago.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.840
Yes, the squatting position is
said to be natural, since it's used

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.280
by so-called primitive peoples
who pass large stools easily,

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:58.080
such that squatting advocates
blame the porcelain throne

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.240
on all manner of Western maladies.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.480
But does the position
really make a difference

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.240
if you're eating the right foods?

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.600
The man who squats because he
has no modern plumbing also tends

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.120
to eat more natural foods that
haven't had the fiber processed out.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.400
Adding fiber to the diet can enable
constipated patients to poop

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.080
effortlessly without having to squat
over some hole in the ground.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:21.360
So maybe if we just change
the design of our diets,

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.400
we don't have to change
the design of our plumbing.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.840
In our next story, we
look at how most people

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:31.360
have between 3 bowel
movements a day

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:33.265
and 3 a week!

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:36.800
But normal doesn’t
necessarily mean optimal.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.440
Ancient Egypt was one
of the great civilizations,

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:43.520
lasting for 3,000 years,

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.400
its knowledge of medicine
vastly underestimated.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.560
They had medical sub-specialties.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.320
The pharaohs, for
example, had access

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:53.360
to dedicated physicians
to be guardians

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:57.920
of the royal bowel movement,
a title alternately translated

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:01.840
from the hieroglyphics to
mean Shepherd of the Anus.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.240
How's that for a resume builder?

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:08.160
Today, the primacy of
its importance continues,

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.640
with some calling for bowel
habits to be considered

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:13.440
a vital sign on how
the body is functioning,

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.360
along with blood pressure,
heart, breathing rate.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.880
Although we may not particularly
like hearing the details

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:19.880
of someone else's
bowel movement,

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:24.080
it is a function that nurses
and doctors need to assess.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:28.400
Surprisingly, the colon remained
relatively unexplored territory,

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:31.040
one of the body's final frontiers.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:35.680
For example, current concepts
of what "normal" stools are like

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.680
primarily emanates from
the detailed records

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:40.800
of 12 consecutive bowel
movements in 27 healthy subjects

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:44.720
from the United Kingdom who boldly
went where no one had gone before.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:48.320
Those must have been
really detailed records.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:51.680
The reason we need
to define normal,

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:54.480
when it comes to bowel movement
frequency, for example,

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:58.160
is how else can you define concepts
like constipation or diarrhea

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:00.240
if you don't know what normal is.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:05.200
Standard physiology textbooks
may not be helpful in this regard

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:07.360
implying that anything
from one bowel movement

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:11.760
every few weeks or months to
24 a day can be regarded as normal.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:14.720
Once every few months?

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:19.200
Of all human bodily
functions defecation

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:22.400
is perhaps the least
understood and least studied.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:28.400
Can't you just ask people? Turns
out people tend to exaggerate.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.040
There's a discrepancy between
what people report

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:34.160
and what researchers find when
they actually have them recorded.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:40.560
It wasn't until 2010 when
we got the first serious look,

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.680
defining normal stool
frequency as between

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:47.120
three per week and three per day,
based on the fact that that's where

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:53.200
98% of people tended to fall. But normal
doesn't necessarily mean optimal.

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:58.000
Having a "normal" salt intake can
lead to a "normal" blood pressure,

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.640
which can help us to die
from all the "normal" causes,

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:01.840
like heart attacks and strokes.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:05.680
Having a normal cholesterol level
in a society where it's normal

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:08.000
to drop dead of heart disease --
our number one killer --

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.200
not necessarily a good thing.

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.800
And indeed significant
proportions of people

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:14.560
with "normal bowel function"

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:17.760
reported urgency, straining,
incomplete defecation,

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:19.840
leading the researchers
to conclude that

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:21.520
that kind of thing must
just be normal.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:26.960
Normal, maybe, if you're
eating a fiber deficient diet.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:30.080
But not normal for our species.

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:32.240
Defecation should not
be a painful exercise.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:34.160
This is readily demonstrable.

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:38.320
For example, the majority of rural
Africans eating their traditional

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.080
fiber-rich plant-based diets

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:43.840
can usually pass without straining
a stool specimen on demand.

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:46.960
See, the rectum may
need to accumulate

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:51.200
4 or 5 ounces of fecal matter before
the defecation reflex is fully initiated,

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:56.000
and so if you don't even build up that
much over the day you'd have to strain

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.840
to prime the rectal pump.

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:01.600
Hippocrates thought
bowel movements

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:04.960
should ideally be two
or three times a day,

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:06.560
which is what you
see in populations

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:10.080
on traditional plant-based diets,
on the kind of fiber intakes

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:14.560
you see in our fellow great apes, and
what may be more representative

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:18.080
of the types of diets we evolved
eating for millions of years.

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:21.680
It seems somewhat
optimistic, though,

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:26.160
to expect the average American
to adopt a rural African diet.

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:31.360
We can, however, eat more
plant-based and bulk up enough

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.560
to take the Hippocratic oath
to go 2 to 3 times a day.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:37.360
No need to obsess about it.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:40.480
In fact there's actually a Bowel
Obsession Syndrome

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:44.640
characterized in part by ideational
rambling over bowel habits,

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:48.640
but three times a day makes sense.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:51.280
We have what's called
a gastrocolic reflex,

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:56.800
which consists of a prompt activation
of muscular waves in our colon

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.960
within 1 to 3 minutes of the ingestion
of the first mouthfuls of food.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:06.160
Even just talking about food can cause
your brain to increase colon activity.

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:10.800
This suggests the body figured
that one meal should be just enough

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.160
to fill you up down there.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:15.840
So maybe we should eat
enough unprocessed plant foods

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:20.000
to get up to three a day, a
movement for every meal.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:26.080
In our final story today,
prunes, figs, and exercise

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:30.240
are put to the test as natural
home remedies for constipation.

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:35.600
The act of defecation involves
a very private sphere

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:38.160
and is the object of cultural
taboos, so much so that

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:41.760
it’s rarely thought of, even by
physicians—but it should be.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:45.320
Constipation accounts for three
million annual visits to doctors

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:48.560
in the United States and
800,000 emergency room visits.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:52.080
Depending on how you define
it, up to 80 percent

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:54.400
of the population may be suffering.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.400
Even people who don’t
think they’re constipated

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.720
may very well be
clinically constipated.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:01.600
A quarter of their so-
called healthy subjects

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:03.760
reported experiencing
incomplete emptying,

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:07.120
and approximately half
indicated increased straining.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.960
In fact, more than
half had found blood

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:10.880
on their toilet paper
within the past year.

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:14.960
In severe cases, the blood
pressure spike associated with

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.840
straining at stool can even
trigger a heart attack or a stroke.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:21.760
There are drugs for it.
There are always drugs,

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.320
resulting in side effects
like headache, nausea, diarrhea,

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:27.920
and abdominal pain, leaving
most patients unsatisfied.

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:31.840
So why not instead just
try to treat the cause?

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:35.440
Common causes of chronic
constipation include lack of

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:38.640
adequate whole plant foods
or insufficient water intake,

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:41.280
and so making changes in the
patient’s diet and lifestyle

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:44.400
is the preferred method for
relieving constipation.

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:47.840
Such nonpharmacological clinical
effective interventions

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:49.280
including engaging in physical

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.280
activity for about 30 minutes a day.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:55.280
A systematic review and meta-
analysis found aerobic exercise

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:59.280
interventions help, starting
at about 140 minutes a week.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:02.080
And then, of course, a diet
centered around whole plant foods,

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:05.200
which are the only naturally
concentrated sources of fiber.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:08.000
Any plants in particular?

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:11.520
If you give elderly women
with severe constipation about

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.560
a dozen prunes a day they
experience significant

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:16.800
improvement within the first week.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:19.680
The control group in the study
wasn’t told to do anything though.

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:21.680
And any time you have one
group doing something and

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:25.520
the other doing nothing, you can’t
discount the placebo effect.

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:28.320
And the placebo response for
constipation trials can range

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:32.000
up to 44 percent, meaning up to
nearly half of the people given

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:35.040
a sugar pill claimed to
experience an improvement.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.680
So, that’s why we need
studies like this.

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:41.600
Subjects were randomized
to about 8 prunes a day

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:45.040
plus a large glass of water;
12 prunes and water;

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:47.680
or just the water alone; so,
even the control group got

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:50.320
an intervention they were told
might help with constipation.

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:54.400
Previous studies mostly
assigned 10 prunes or so a day,

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:57.040
so the researchers wanted to
see if more was better or less

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:00.960
was sufficient and...they found
a significant improvement

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:03.920
in stool bulk on the prunes
and a significant increase

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:06.960
in bowel movement frequency,
though no real difference

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:10.240
between 8 and 12; so,
8 a day seems sufficient.

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:13.920
Prunes even appear superior
to psyllium, sold as Metamucil,

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:17.520
beating it out in terms of improved
stool frequency and consistency.

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.880
We used to think it was
just all the fiber in prunes

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:24.320
that was helping, but prune
juice evidently works too,

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:27.680
which, like most juices,
has had the fiber removed.

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:31.920
Other potential active components
include a natural sugar alcohol

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:35.680
known as sorbitol that’s
used in some sugar-free gum.

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:39.040
Once you eat more than a dozen
or so large prunes a day, however,

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:42.240
the dose of sorbitol could
start reaching laxative levels

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:45.200
in susceptible individuals.
So, be careful.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:49.200
If you don’t have constipation,
should you avoid prunes?

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:52.480
That’s been put to the test, and...
most people should

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:55.680
be able to eat a dozen or
so a day without any issues.

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:57.760
In fact, it’s interesting to
note that prunes have been

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:02.720
traditionally used as both a
laxative and an antidiarrheal remedy.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:05.920
What about dried figs? One
of the few medicinal plants

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:07.760
mentioned explicitly in the Bible.

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:11.600
Researchers took patients with the
type of irritable bowel syndrome

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:15.040
characterized by constipation
and randomized them to one fig

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:18.480
with breakfast and one fig with
lunch, each with a glass of water,

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:21.120
and there was a significant improvement
in frequency of defecation

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:24.720
and a significant drop in
the frequency of hard stools,

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:28.800
compared to control. Ah, but
what was the control?

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:31.520
The control group was just asked
to continue their normal diet.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:34.240
In other words, to
do nothing special.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:38.400
The placebo response for
irritable bowel is infamous.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:42.480
Give people with IBS a fake sugar
pill, and sometimes 72 percent

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.320
say they magically feel better.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:46.160
That’s why we need
this kind of study:

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:49.440
a randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial.

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:52.960
Researchers made a gross-
sounding fig paste placebo

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:54.960
that supposedly had
the same taste, smell,

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:56.160
and appearance as the real deal.

00:13:56.720 --> 00:13:59.040
Those who got the real
figs, about six a day,

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.400
seemed to improve colon transit
time, stool consistency,

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:05.520
and abdominal discomfort
compared to the placebo.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:09.520
Researchers measured transit
time by having people swallow

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:12.720
little beads that would show up
on x-rays so they could track

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:15.040
the progress thorough
their digestive system.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.600
They found that those eating
the real figs sped up their

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:19.760
gut movement by a full 24 hours

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:23.520
Defecation frequency per week
didn’t beat out placebo though,

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:25.920
and in fact, they tested
so many different outcomes

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:28.640
even the stool consistency
and tummy discomfort results

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:30.160
may have been statistical flukes.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:35.262
So, it looks like prunes would
be the better treatment choice.

